<a href="/encyclopedia/alhflaed"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alhflaed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alhflæd</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alhflæd was a daughter of King Oswiu of Northumbria who married Peada, ruler of the Middle Angles, around 653, on condition that he accept baptism.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alhfrith"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alhfrith.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alhfrith</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alhfrith was a son of King Oswiu of Northumbria who ruled Deira as sub-king under his father from about 655.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alhred-of-northumbria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alhred-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alhred of Northumbria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alhred was king of Northumbria from 765 to 774, during a period of rapid royal turnover.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alhucemas-landing"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alhucemas-landing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alhucemas landing</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1925</span><span class="enc-snip">The Alhucemas landing was an amphibious assault by Spanish forces, supported by France, on the bay of Alhucemas (Al Hoceima) in northern Morocco in September 1925.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-abdullah-saleh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Abdullah Saleh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Abdullah Saleh was President of North Yemen from 1978 and, after unification in 1990, the first President of the Republic of Yemen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-abu-hassun"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-abu-hassun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Abu Hassun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Abu Hassun was the last Wattasid ruler of Morocco.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-adil-shah-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Adil Shah I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Adil Shah I was the fifth Adil Shahi sultan of Bijapur, ruling from 1558 to 1580.</span></a></li></ul>
